  "snippet": "Resolution Source\n\nResolver\n\nForecast models from the Japan Meteorological Agency and international ensembles indicate Tokyo’s May 29 maximum will likely peak near 29–30 °C, with a modest chance of exceeding 31 °C if daytime heating intensifies under clearer skies. Late-May climatology shows average highs around 27 °C, but urban heat-island effects, variable Pacific high pressure, and sea-breeze timing can easily shift the peak by 1–2 °C. Ensemble spread remains the dominant uncertainty factor, as small changes in cloud cover or wind direction alter surface energy balance enough to differentiate the closely matched 29 °C and 30 °C outcomes.\n\n## Rules\n\n## Market Context\n\nResolution Source\n\nResolver [...] ## Rules\n\n## Market Context\n\nResolution Source\n\nResolver\n\nForecast models from the Japan Meteorological Agency and international ensembles indicate Tokyo’s May 29 maximum will likely peak near 29–30 °C, with a modest chance of exceeding 31 °C if daytime heating intensifies under clearer skies. Late-May climatology shows average highs around 27 °C, but urban heat-island effects, variable Pacific high pressure, and sea-breeze timing can easily shift the peak by 1–2 °C. Ensemble spread remains the dominant uncertainty factor, as small changes in cloud cover or wind direction alter surface energy balance enough to differentiate the closely matched 29 °C and 30 °C outcomes.\n\n### Related\n\nicon for Ethereum Up or Down\n\nEthereum Up or Down\n\nicon for Ethereum Up or Down\n\nEthereum Up or Down [...] 30°C\n\n$1,836 Vol.\n\n32%\n\n31°C or higher\n\n$3,916 Vol.\n\n21%\n\n29°C 40%\n\n30°C 32%\n\n31°C or higher 21%\n\n28°C 12%\n\n$37,504 Vol.\n\n$37,504 Vol.\n\n21°C or below\n\n<1%\n\n22°C\n\n<1%\n\n23°C\n\n<1%\n\n24°C\n\n<1%\n\n25°C\n\n<1%\n\n26°C\n\n<1%\n\n27°C\n\n1%\n\n28°C\n\n12%\n\n29°C\n\n40%\n\n30°C\n\n32%\n\n31°C or higher\n\n21%\n\n## Rules\n\n## Market Context\n\nMarket Opened: May 27, 2026, 12:06 AM ET\n\nResolution Source\n\nRes